{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 7, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a medieval nobleman and the ruler of the County of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187 He was a member of the House of Anjou and a grandson of Fulk V Count of Anjou\n\n* **Early Life ** \nRaymond III was born around 1140 in Anjou France He was the son of William I Count of Poitou and his first wife Adele de Châtillon Raymond later married Beatrice of Ibelin and then Berengaria of Navarre\n\n* **Reign as Count of Tripoli ** \nRaymond III became the Count of Tripoli in 1152 after the death of his cousin Pagan the Cruel He ruled the county with his brothers Amalric I and Esclarmonde Fulk V Count of Anjou had granted Raymond the county as a fief\n\n* **First Crusade ** \nRaymond III played an important role in the First Crusade He joined the expedition to Jerusalem in 1147 and participated in the Siege of Antioch in 1148 Raymond was also present at the Battle of Ascalon in 1153\n\n* **Defenses of Tripoli ** \nDuring his reign Raymond III strengthened the defenses of Tripoli He built walls and fortifications around the city and expanded the port of Tripoli to increase trade\n\n* **Expulsion of Fatimids ** \nRaymond III launched a successful campaign against the Fatimid Caliphate in 1163 and 1165 He captured the port city of Sidon and defeated the Fatimid forces at the Battle of Mersivan\n\n* **Death ** \nRaymond III died on 28 July 1187 during the Third Crusade He was killed in the Battle of Hattin while fighting alongside King Guy of Lusignan and King Amalric I Raymond III was succeeded by his brother Amalric I", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0011805477552115917}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.00011586471373448148}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.19920571148395538}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.802703940891661e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob"